# Line endings are normalised on commit, so a checkout on Windows does not turn
# every file into a diff, and the ASCII-only rule in AGENTS.md is not quietly
# broken by a stray CR.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The icons are binary. git-lfs keeps them out of the packfile, and the `-text`
# marker stops git from ever trying to reconcile two versions line by line.
#
# Any workflow that reads these files must check out with `lfs: true`. Without
# it the working tree holds a pointer file, and the documentation build then
# ships a few lines of text where an image was expected -- which fails as a
# broken image rather than as a missing file, so it is worth stating here.
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ico filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# One exemption, and it is not a matter of taste. DOCKERHUB.md points Docker
# Hub's overview image at
# raw.githubusercontent.com/lorem-dev/doppel/main/assets/icon-128.png, and that
# endpoint serves the LFS *pointer* rather than the bytes -- verified on
# 2026-08-11, 130 bytes of ASCII beginning "version
# https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1". Tracked through LFS, the overview would
# render a broken image, and nothing in this repository would fail to say so.
# This file is small enough that a plain blob costs nothing.
assets/icon-128.png -filter -diff -merge text=auto

# The documentation's screenshots, for the same reason as the icons: a new
# screenshot is a new whole file rather than a diff, and every UI change brings
# one. `docs/screenshots/` is read only by the mkdocs build, whose workflow
# checks out with `lfs: true` -- without that it would ship the pointer file as
# a broken image.
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# An SVG is XML, and a readable diff is worth more than treating it as opaque.
*.svg text
